# divemate-cli configuration
#
# Copy to:  ~/.config/divemate-cli/config
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/divemate-cli
#   cp config.example ~/.config/divemate-cli/config
#
# This file is sourced by the `dmcli` wrapper as shell, so it is plain
# KEY="value" lines (and you may use $HOME, command substitution, etc).
# A variable already set in your environment overrides the value here, so you can
# still do:  DIVEMATE_DB=/tmp/other.ddb dmcli list
#
# Override the config path itself with the DIVEMATE_CONFIG env var.

# --- Local logbook -----------------------------------------------------------

# Where your DiveMate .ddb lives (and where `pull` downloads it).
DIVEMATE_DB="$HOME/dives/DiveMate.ddb"

# Container image tag to run (rarely needed).
#DIVEMATE_IMAGE="localhost/divemate-cli:latest"

# --- Google Drive sync (used by `dmcli pull`) --------------------------------

# Path to the service-account JSON key.
DIVEMATE_GDRIVE_KEY="$HOME/.config/divemate-cli/service-account.json"

# ID of the shared Drive folder (the part after /folders/ in its URL).
DIVEMATE_GDRIVE_FOLDER="xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"

# Remote file name to look for in that folder (default: DiveMate.ddb).
#DIVEMATE_GDRIVE_FILE="DiveMate.ddb"
